---

Root cause (same shape as Fix A / the prior dfmgr.c fix, commit 9db33b7674):

ThreadedGUCUnlock() (guc.c, pre-fix) ended with an unconditional
RESUME_INTERRUPTS() after the outermost pthread_mutex_unlock()/xtc_amutex_unlock().
The locked region (set_config_with_handle_internal(), reached from every SET
statement) routinely calls ereport(ERROR) on ordinary conditions (invalid value,
permission check, custom GUC check-hook rejection).  errfinish() unconditionally
resets InterruptHoldoffCount to 0 while unwinding ANY error (elog.c), and that
reset can run BEFORE the PG_FINALLY block's ThreadedGUCUnlock() call does.  By
the time RESUME_INTERRUPTS() ran, InterruptHoldoffCount could legitimately
already be 0, tripping Assert(InterruptHoldoffCount > 0).

Fix applied: identical pattern to reloptions.c/dfmgr.c -- tolerate
InterruptHoldoffCount already being 0 (an intervening error unwind reset it);
only decrement if there is something to undo.

AFTER the fix: `gmake check-threaded-pooled`'s full parallel_schedule run got
further (reached mcxt.c's unrelated pre-existing "parent->firstchild == context"
assert, a third and separate bug -- see FIXA_GUC_C_SIDE_FIX.md), and the
narrower reloptions/guc/xml/xml2-only schedule (which avoids the domain/FK
tests that trip the mcxt.c bug) ran clean: see
.ec2/relx-20260910/fixA/, .ec2/relx-20260910/fixB/.
